     <h1 class="title" title="Kalimpong Hill Station">Kalimpong</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/east-india-hill-stations/kalimpong-hill-station.jpg" title="Kalimpong hill station" alt="Kalimpong hill station, hill stations in india, east india hill stations, Kalimpong" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> West Bengal<br />
<b>Area:</b> 780 sq.Kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Bustling Bazaars<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 1250m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 16&#176;C - 24&#176;C, Winter 5&#176;C - 15&#176;C <br/>
<b>Best time to visit:</b> March to June, September to November</p>     
<p><b>Main Attractions:</b> Mountains of Eastern Himalaya, Near Bhutan , Tibet Border</p>
<p>Located at an altitude of 1800 meters on the border of Bhutan, Tibet and Sikkim in the eastern Himalayas, Darjeeling, Kalimpong sub-division city was an important commercial center in the early days, when trade routes / routes silk between Tibet, Bhutan and Sikkim were very active. The <b>climate of Kalimpong</b> bright attracted the British, who later established their settlements there. The old church, the house of Graham, <b>Morgan Casa de Campo golf course</b> still retain the memory of the British Empire. Once a small village <b>Leptcha</b> slowly transformed into an ideal place to holydayers.</p>





